;pl0 : zero power (0W)
;pl1 : f1 channel - power level for hard pulse (default)
;pl2 : f2 channel - power level for hard pulse (default)
;plw10 : f1 channel - power level for TOCSY transfer
;sp12 : f1 channel - power level of refocusing shaped pulse
;spw14 : f2 channel - power level of inversion shaped pulse
;spw15 : f2 channel - power level of time-reversed inversion shaped pulse
;sp29: power level for shaped pulse (adiabatic)
;sp37: power levelr for shaped pulse 180 degree of psyche element (Crp_psyche.20)

;p1 : f1 channel - 90 degree high power pulse 
;p2 : f1 channel - 180 degree high power pulse
;p3 : f2 channel - 90 degree high power pulse
;p4 : f2 channel - 180 degree high power pulse
;p6 : f1 channel - 90 degree low power pulse for TOCSY
;p8 : f1 channel - Spherical randomization pulse [1-1.5 msec]
;p12 : f1 channel - 180 degree refocusing shaped pulse
;p14 : f2 channel - 180 degree inversion shaped pulse
;p15 : f2 channel - 180 degree inversion shaped pulse
;p32: 180 degree shaped pulse (adiabatic)    [20 msec]
;     smoothed chirp (sweepwidth, 20% smoothing, 10000 points)
;p45 : f1 channel - duration of double-chirp PSYCHE pulse element [30 ms]

;p11 : duration of weak gradient during PSYCHE pulse element [p11=p10]
;p16 : duration of CTP gradients [200 us - 1 ms] 
;p17 : duration of CTP gradients [1 ms]
;p18 : homospoil gradient [1 msec]

;d0 : chemical shift evolution for pure shift
;d1 : relaxation delay; [5*T1 s]
;d4 : delay for J(HX) evolvution
;d9 : TOCSY mixing time [50-200 ms]
;d11 : delay for disk I/O [30 msec]
;d16 : recovery delay for echo gradients 
;d24: chunk duration [10-25 ms]
;DELTA: total duration of reconstructed FID

;spnam12 : f1 channel - file name for the selective 180 refocusing shaped pulse [RSNOB]
;spnam24 : f2 channel - file name for the selective 180 inversion shaped pulse [Iburp2]
;spnam25 : f2 channel - file name for the selective 180 inversion shaped pulse [Iburp2]
;spnam32 : f1 channel - file name for the adiabatic shaped pulse using in first ZQF [CHIRP]
; smoothed chirp (low to high, 20% smoothing, 1000 points, 20KHz)
;spnam34 : f1 channel - file name for the adiabatic shaped pulse using in last ZQF [CHIRP]
; smoothed chirp (low to high, 20% smoothing, 1000 points, 20KHz)
;spnam37 : f1 channel - file name for double-chirp PSYCHE pulse element [SALTIRE]

;cnst2: selected J(HX) (in Hz)
;cnst3 : number of X coupled with selected proton 
;cnst6: bandwidth of TOCSY transfer
;cnst12: f1 channel - bandwidth for selective refocussing pulse (in Hz)
;cnst14: f2 channel - bandwidth for selective inversion pulse (in Hz)
;cnst15: f2 channel - chemical shift for selective inversion 19F pulse (in ppm) 
;cnst16: f2 channel - chemical shift for selective refocussing 1H pulse (in ppm)
;cnst20 : desired flip angle for PSYCHE pulse element (degree) [10-25] 
;cnst21 : bandwidth of each chirp in PSYCHE pulse element (Hz) [10000 Hz]
;cnst53: GammaB1 of first adiabatic ZQF shaped pulse 
;cnst54: GammaB1 of last adiabatic ZQF shaped pulse 
;cnst60: sweepwidth of single chirp element in Crp_psyche.20 in Hz [10000]
;cnst61: desired flip angle in degree (ca. 20)
;cnst62: gammaB1/2PI value for p49:sp37 (in Hz)
;cnst63: scaling factor for power (sp37)

;l30: number of complex points at the beginning not to be included 
;        in reconstruction
;l31: number of complex points along the acquisition dimension per block
;BETA: flip angle (ca. 20 degree)
;SWi: sweep width in the pseudo dimension 
;        should be 2 to 3 times the width of the widest multiplett
;in0: = dw*l31

;l1 : loop for DIPSI cycle: ((p6*115.112) * l1) = mixing time
;ns: 8 * n, total number of scans: NS * TD0
;ds: 8
;td1 : number of t1 increments for pure shift dimension
;in0 : 1/(2 * SW) = DW
;nd0 : 2
;MC2 : QF


;for z-only gradients:
;gpz0 :  3%  (first ZQF gradient [1-3%])
;gpz1 : 13%  (CTP gradient)
;gpz2 : 49%  (Spoil gradient)
;gpz3 : 79%  (CTP gradient)
;gpz4 : 43%  (CTP gradient)
;gpz8 : 31%  (CTP gradient)
;gpz10:  3%  (last ZQF gradient [1-3%])
;gpz11:  1%  (PSYCHE ZQF gradient [1-3%])

